    <bpmn:process id="W_W589" name="W589. Weekly Cash Flow Forecast &amp; Treasury Planning" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Weekly treasury planning cycle (every Monday)
Frequency: Weekly (rolling 4-week forward forecast updated every Monday)
Volume: 5 legal entities consolidated; ~PHP 5.19B/month gross cash inflows across 200 stores (cash ~42%, card ~36%, e-wallet ~15%, corporate/charge ~5%, online ~3% per profile §5); ~PHP 3.8–4.0B/month outflows (vendor payments ~PHP 2.5B, payroll ~PHP 230M, import LC/TT ~PHP 600M, Capex ~PHP 200M, taxes ~PHP 300M); ~210 bank accounts across 4 banking partners (BDO, BPI, Metrobank, Chinabank)
Owner: Treasury Analyst
Participants: Treasury Analyst, Treasury Manager, CFO (A for surplus/deficit actions), AP Supervisor (C for payment schedule), Payroll Manager (C for payroll dates), Import Coordinator (C for LC calendar), Store Operations Finance (C for store collection data), Controller (I)
Source: workflow W589 — Weekly Cash Flow Forecast &amp; Treasury Planning</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W589_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W589_Lane1" name="Treasury Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W589_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W589_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W589_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W589_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W589_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W589_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W589_Task18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W589_Task19</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W589_Task20</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W589_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W589_Lane2" name="AP Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W589_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W589_Lane3" name="Payroll Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W589_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W589_Lane4" name="Import Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W589_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W589_Lane5" name="Treasury Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W589_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W589_End21</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W589_Start7" name="Weekly treasury planning cycle (every Monday)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W589_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W589_Task8" name="Prior week actual vs. forecast variance analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Prior week actual vs. forecast variance analysis: Treasury Analyst pulls prior week&#x27;s actual cash inflows and outflows from banking platform; compares to prior week&#x27;s forecast; documents material variances (&gt;±5% of forecast per entity) with root cause — common causes include: delayed store deposits, unexpected vendor early-payment discounts taken, payroll overtime variance, import shipment timing changes
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 45 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W589_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W589_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W589_Task9" name="Store cash collection aggregation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Store cash collection aggregation: System aggregates prior week&#x27;s store-level collections by payment method — cash (PHP ~2.08B/month across 200 stores), card (settled via BDO/BPI acquiring, net of MDR 1.5–2.5%), e-wallet (GCash/Maya, settled T+1 net of 1.0–1.5% fee), online payments (via Digital Commerce Inc., settled T+3–5); Treasury Analyst reviews collection efficiency — cash deposit shortfall rate target &lt;0.5%, card settlement completeness, e-wallet reconciliation exceptions per W261
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W589_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W589_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W589_Task10" name="AP payment forecast (vendor payment run schedule)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: AP payment forecast (vendor payment run schedule): AP Supervisor provides upcoming vendor payment run schedule — standard payment runs on 10th and 25th of month per W556; early-pay discount opportunities (2/10 net 30 terms from major suppliers); overdue/past-due invoices requiring priority payment per W7; one-time payments (insurance premiums, lease deposits, utilities); total AP payment forecast for 4-week window
Responsible (R): AP Supervisor
Accountable (A): Treasury Analyst
Duration: 20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W589_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W589_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W589_Task11" name="Payroll forecast">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Payroll forecast: Payroll Manager provides payroll forecast for 4-week window — semi-monthly payroll on the 15th and 30th (~PHP 110–120M per run covering ~6,911 employees); variable components: overtime, commissions, 13th month accrual release (November–December), statutory contributions due per agency calendars (SSS by the last day of the following month per RA 11199; PhilHealth and Pag-IBIG by the 10th of the following month); special payroll runs (separation pay, backpay adjustments)
Responsible (R): Payroll Manager
Accountable (A): Treasury Analyst
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W589_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W589_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W589_Task12" name="Intercompany settlement forecast">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Intercompany settlement forecast: Treasury Analyst maps intercompany cash flows for 4-week window — monthly IC settlements on 5th per W14: Logistics Inc. → Depot Inc. (store replenishment freight), Digital Commerce Inc. → Depot Inc. (ecommerce payment collection remittance), Depot Inc. → Holdings Inc. (management fees), Property Mgmt Inc. → Holdings Inc. (lease income); IC loan interest payments per W137; IC dividend declarations (quarterly, if applicable); system auto-generates IC settlement calendar from open IC balances
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W589_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W589_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W589_Task13" name="LC/import payment calendar">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: LC/import payment calendar: Import Coordinator provides LC payment schedule — open LCs with maturity dates in 4-week window per W232; TT payments for non-LC imports; customs duties and taxes per W239/W464; FX conversion requirements (PHP → USD) for import payments; total import payment forecast for 4-week window with PHP equivalents at current spot rate
Responsible (R): Import Coordinator
Accountable (A): Treasury Analyst
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W589_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W589_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W589_Task14" name="FX exposure review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: FX exposure review: Treasury Analyst updates FX exposure report — total USD-denominated payables outstanding (import POs confirmed per W2B), USD bank balances across 5 import accounts, open forward contracts per W80 with maturity dates and forward rates, net unhedged USD exposure; calculates potential FX gain/loss on unhedged exposure using current BDO/BPI USD/PHP spot rate; flags if unhedged exposure exceeds 30-day rolling average import payment threshold per W30.10a FX hedging policy
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W589_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W589_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W589_Task15" name="4-week rolling forecast compilation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: 4-week rolling forecast compilation: Treasury Analyst compiles complete 4-week rolling cash flow forecast per entity and consolidated — Week 1 (high confidence, based on committed payables and confirmed receivables), Week 2 (medium confidence, based on scheduled payments and historical collection patterns), Weeks 3–4 (lower confidence, based on forecasted sales, historical payment patterns, and known commitments); forecast includes: opening balance per entity, scheduled inflows (store collections, AR collections per W8, IC receipts), scheduled outflows (AP payments, payroll, import payments, IC payments, tax payments per W90, capex per W21), projected closing balance per entity and consolidated
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W589_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W589_Flow32</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W589_Task16" name="Cash surplus/deficit action plan">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Cash surplus/deficit action plan: Treasury Analyst identifies projected surplus or deficit positions per entity — (a) Surplus: recommend short-term placement (BDO/BPI time deposit, 7–30 day tenor, current PHP interest rate environment); calculate opportunity cost of idle cash vs. placement yield; (b) Deficit: recommend credit line drawdown from existing PHP 3B revolving credit facility (RCF) with BDO/BPI syndicated; calculate interest cost of drawdown; identify payment deferral opportunities (AP terms negotiation with non-critical vendors); (c) Inter-entity optimization: if Entity A has surplus and Entity B has deficit in same week, recommend inter-entity cash transfer per W14 instead of external borrowing or placement
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W589_Flow32</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W589_Flow33</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W589_Task17" name="Forecast review and approval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Forecast review and approval: Treasury Manager reviews complete forecast package (variance analysis, collection data, AP/payroll/import calendars, FX exposure, 4-week projection, action plan); validates assumptions; challenges optimistic collection estimates or conservative payment assumptions; approves action plan items; escalates to CFO for items requiring approval: credit line drawdown &gt;PHP 100M, short-term placement &gt;PHP 200M, inter-entity transfer &gt;PHP 50M
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W589_Flow33</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W589_Flow34</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W589_Task18" name="Action plan execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 11: Action plan execution: Treasury Analyst executes approved actions — (a) initiates short-term time deposit placements via BDO/BPI corporate banking platform; (b) submits credit line drawdown request to bank; (c) executes inter-entity transfers per approved schedule; (d) coordinates with AP Supervisor on payment timing adjustments (defer non-critical vendor payments from Week 2 to Week 3 if deficit projected); (e) executes FX conversions for confirmed import payments at optimal timing within week; (f) all actions logged in treasury management system with audit trail
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W589_Flow34</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W589_Flow35</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W589_Task19" name="Distribution and communication">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 12: Distribution and communication: Treasury Analyst distributes approved forecast to: CFO (executive summary), Controller (for close process planning), AP Supervisor (payment schedule confirmation), Payroll Manager (payroll funding confirmation), Import Coordinator (FX conversion schedule); system auto-archives forecast version for historical tracking and forecast accuracy measurement
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W589_Flow35</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W589_Flow36</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W589_Task20" name="Mid-week update (Thursday)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 13: Mid-week update (Thursday): If material events occur between Monday forecast and Thursday (large unexpected payment, significant collection shortfall, FX rate movement &gt;2%, emergency Capex approval), Treasury Analyst issues abbreviated mid-week flash update to Treasury Manager and CFO with revised Week 1–2 projection
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 15 min (as needed)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W589_Flow36</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W589_Flow37</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W589_End21" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W589_Flow37</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W589_Annotation22">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-293 (ensure controlled execution — Cash Positioning &amp; Forecasting (PA-18.1).) | - operational: Treasury Analyst review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Treasury Analyst</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W589_Assoc23" sourceRef="W589_Annotation22" targetRef="W589_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
